WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.220
$20 BILLION:
Apple has always been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:07.020
infamous for their high prices and large profit&nbsp;
margins. While the rest of the manufacturing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:14.400
industry has net margins of 2-5%, Apple has a net&nbsp;
margin of 25%. But, over the past couple of years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:20.520
they’ve taken this to the even next level. Of&nbsp;
course, they’ve jacked up prices of iPhones and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:26.940
introduced high margin services but I’m talking&nbsp;
about something much more profitable. I’m talking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:33.000
about the largest brand placement operation&nbsp;
that has ever taken place. If you use an iPhone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:37.740
Safari and Siri have probably redirected&nbsp;
you to Google tens of thousands of times.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:44.400
This probably felt quite natural given that&nbsp;
Google is the most dominant search engine. I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:50.400
imagine if Apple had always redirected you to&nbsp;
Bing. That would’ve felt so wrong but that may&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:55.320
have actually been more likely than you might&nbsp;
think. You see, Apple didn’t choose to integrate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.320 --> 00:01:00.840
Google just because it was the popular choice or&nbsp;
to diss Microsoft. The only reason they decided to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:06.360
integrate Google was because they were willing to&nbsp;
pay them. At first, it was a much more reasonable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:13.560
amount. In 2014, it was about a billion dollars.&nbsp;
But since then, this number hasn’t doubled or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:21.360
tripled or even quintupled, it has straight up&nbsp;
grown 20X to $20 billion. And the best part is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:27.720
that this is basically 100% profit for Apple.&nbsp;
For perspective, the iPhone user count has only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:34.020
grown by about 3X during the same time period. So,&nbsp;
Google is paying over 6 times more for each user.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:40.440
This is not only a ridiculous amount to pay for&nbsp;
search engine integration but it’s a ridiculous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:47.640
amount even for Apple as a whole. Apple makes&nbsp;
between $95 to $100 billion every year. So, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:53.940
$20 billion that Google is paying them literally&nbsp;
accounts for 20% of Apple’s entire net profit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.940 --> 00:02:00.240
In other words, Apple could reduce everything else&nbsp;
they do to a breakeven operation and just based&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:07.260
on the royalty from Google, they would boast a&nbsp;
valuation of $600 billion aka world’s 10th largest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:14.520
company. And this massive payment just scratches&nbsp;
the surface of Apple’s mega monetization plan. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:19.620
join me as we take a look at Apple’s brilliant&nbsp;
strategy to outlive the stagnation of the iPhone.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:26.160
iPHONE DEPENDENCY:
We all know that Apple’s biggest product is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:32.160
the iPhone and that it’s still the core of their&nbsp;
business, but do you know just how dependent they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:38.580
really are? Well, in the first quarter of this&nbsp;
year, Apple pulled in a total of $94.8 billion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:45.600
worth of revenue. But, out of this $94.8 billion,&nbsp;
$51 billion was directly from iPhone sales. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:51.720
other words, over half of Apple’s entire revenue&nbsp;
still comes from selling iPhones. This becomes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:55.860
even worse when you consider that the rest of&nbsp;
their revenue is directly linked to the iPhone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.860 --> 00:03:01.320
Sure, Apple might have hundreds of millions of&nbsp;
users for iCloud and Apple Music and the App Store&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:07.620
but how many of these people would still use these&nbsp;
services if they didn’t have an iPhone. The same&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:11.940
thing could be said about Apple’s other physical&nbsp;
products as well. How many people buy an Apple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:17.820
Watch and a Macbook just because they’ve already&nbsp;
bought into the Apple ecosystem? So, despite being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.820 --> 00:03:24.180
a $3 trillion company, Apple is still like 90%&nbsp;
dependent on their hero product: the iPhone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:32.400
This is a massive problem because iPhone sales&nbsp;
peaked way back in 2015 which is somehow almost a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:37.980
decade ago at this point. And it’s no wonder why.&nbsp;
Smartphones have basically reached their peak form&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:43.980
which makes it less and less appealing to upgrade&nbsp;
with every iteration. But there is a silver lining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:49.020
to all of this. While Apple is selling less&nbsp;
iPhones in total, the people who do buy iPhones&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:55.020
nowadays tend to be people who are converting&nbsp;
from Android. In fact, back in 2016, iPhones only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.020 --> 00:04:01.560
accounted for 33% of smartphones sales in the US.&nbsp;
But, by the end of 2020, this number had nearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:06.060
doubled to 65%. This is not just the case in the&nbsp;
US. Apple is setting records in China and they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.060 --> 00:04:11.340
just recently started opening stores in India as&nbsp;
well. So, while Apple has had a tough time getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:16.140
people to upgrade their iPhones, they’ve actually&nbsp;
done really well in terms of retaining iPhone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:22.260
users and getting Android users to switch teams.&nbsp;
So, the key for Apple has very much been to focus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.260 --> 00:04:28.260
on monetizing existing iPhone users as opposed to&nbsp;
selling more iPhones which brings us into phase&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:33.840
1 of Apple’s monetization strategy. Given that&nbsp;
Apple is very much a hardware company as much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:38.640
as they are a software company, they started off&nbsp;
with launching smartphone adjacent products. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:44.040
of course includes smartphone cases, the Apple&nbsp;
Watch, Airpods, and AirTags. At first, many of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:49.740
these products got quite a bit of resistance&nbsp;
especially the Airpods. Paying $150 for a pair&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:56.040
of wireless headphones seemed ludicrous 6 years&nbsp;
ago. But nowadays, that’s the norm. In fact, you’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.040 --> 00:05:00.480
probably be the odd one out if you were using&nbsp;
wired headphones in public. Around the same time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:05.700
Apple also experimented with pricing. They were&nbsp;
very much pushing the boundaries of what people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:11.880
were willing to pay for iPhone. What started&nbsp;
off as a $650 phone rose to $750 and $800 and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:17.160
a $1000 and eventually $1100 which is where the&nbsp;
pro max starts now. They’ve actually chilled out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:22.620
on raising prices for 5 years now but there are&nbsp;
rumors that the iPhone 15 will have a $100 price&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:28.500
increase so this may not last for much longer.&nbsp;
No matter how many times Apple increase iPhone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:33.240
prices though, there’s only so much profit&nbsp;
that can be made from hardware given that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:37.620
you have to pay for factories and materials and&nbsp;
logistics and shipping and all of that. Software&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:43.140
on the other hand is far more lucrative which&nbsp;
brings us into phase 2 of Apple’s grand plan.

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:46.620
MONETIZE MONETIZE MONETIZE:&nbsp;

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:51.960
Apple has taken a completely different approach&nbsp;
when it comes to software. With hardware,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:57.180
they always positioned themselves as the premium&nbsp;
brand with the premium products that came in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.180 --> 00:06:02.400
at a premium price. But with software, they’ve&nbsp;
positioned themselves extremely compeititvely.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:09.000
In fact, in most cases, their pricing is identical&nbsp;
to the compeition. Take iCloud for example. Apple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:17.400
charges $1 for 50 GB, $3 for 200 GB, and $10 for&nbsp;
2 TB. Now, guess what Google charges for cloud&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:24.420
storage. Well, their basic plans starts at 100&nbsp;
GB for $2 which is the same as $1 for 50 GB. From&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.420 --> 00:06:31.200
there, they have the same 200 GB for $3 and 2 TB&nbsp;
for $10. The same thing can be said about Apple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:38.580
Music as well. For student plans, Spotify charges&nbsp;
$5 while Apple charges $6. For individual plans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:46.140
Spotify charges $10 while Apple charges $11. And&nbsp;
for family plans, Spofity charges $16 while Apple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:52.680
charges $17. Till the end of last year, this small&nbsp;
$1 pricing discrepancy wasn’t even a thing either.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:58.200
This has given Apple a pretty unique monopoly.&nbsp;
While there’s nothing fundamentally special&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:02.820
about Apple’s services in terms of pricing or&nbsp;
features, given that their entire brand image&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:07.260
has been built around premium products, people&nbsp;
naturally associate Apple’s services with being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:11.940
superior as well even if they aren’t. So, when the&nbsp;
average iPhone user is choosing between Spotify&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.940 --> 00:07:17.880
and Apple Music or iCloud and Google Drive, they&nbsp;
tend to just go with the Apple’s offering. This is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:21.900
only propelled by the fact that Apple’s offerings&nbsp;
tend to have better integration with Apple’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:28.200
devices well for obvious reasons. This has allowed&nbsp;
Apple to reach just a ridiculous number of paid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:35.340
subscribers, over 900 million to be exact. For&nbsp;
perspective, even Netflix only has a total of 232&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.340 --> 00:07:40.260
million subscribers and getting paid subscribers&nbsp;
is literally their main business. For Apple,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:46.320
it’s a sidequest. This number becomes even crazier&nbsp;
when you consider that there’s “only” 1.36 billion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:52.020
iPhone users. This means that nearly 70% of&nbsp;
all iPhone users have some sort of paid Apple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:57.720
subscription. Now of course, this isn’t exactly&nbsp;
true as Apple’s most dedicated userbase likely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.720 --> 00:08:03.480
has multiple Apple subscriptions which skews the&nbsp;
numbers but you get the idea. Apple is killing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:09.180
it with services and that’s just the obvious&nbsp;
services. We can’t talk about Apple’s services&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.180 --> 00:08:16.620
without mentioning the almighty App Store which&nbsp;
literally has a trillion dollar GDP. If the Apple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:22.080
App Store was a country, they would have the 16th&nbsp;
highest GDP in the world. Now, Apple doesn’t get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:26.640
a commission on most of this activity as most&nbsp;
of it doesn’t go directly through Apple. But,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:32.220
for the transactions that do pass through Apple,&nbsp;
they collect a solid 15 to 30% which translates&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:38.700
to somewhere between $70 and 85 billion. And&nbsp;
given that shipping software is magnitudes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:44.460
cheaper than shipper hardware, this is far more&nbsp;
profitable for Apple than selling iPhones. Going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:49.800
back to the first quarter of 2023, services only&nbsp;
accounted for about a fifth of Apple’s revenue.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:55.860
In terms of gross profit, however, services&nbsp;
accounted for over a third and this is only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.860 --> 00:09:01.860
growing by the day. Before you know it, services&nbsp;
will account for over half of Apple’s profit but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:06.960
all of that is nothing in comparison to Apple’s&nbsp;
real money driver which brings us into phase 3.

00:09:06.960 --> 00:09:12.960
THE WALLED GARDEN:
When people refer to Apple’s products,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:18.240
they often talk about a walled garden. For&nbsp;
obvious reasons, Apple likes to promote people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:22.980
to use Apple products over other products.&nbsp;
So, they tend to make their integrations with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:27.180
third party products substantially worse than&nbsp;
the integrations with their own products like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.180 --> 00:09:33.000
iMessage and Facetime. This has prompted many&nbsp;
users to go with Apple for everything. This in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:37.500
itself is a pretty smart strategy in terms of&nbsp;
getting more customers and increasing loyalty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:44.340
but it goes much deeper than just that. All of a&nbsp;
sudden, the only way to reach certain people is to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.340 --> 00:09:49.500
go through Apple as they’ve made it substantially&nbsp;
harder for other companies to track iPhone users.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:55.380
They like to brand this as a privacy effort and&nbsp;
I’m sure that’s part of the equation but the other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.380 --> 00:10:01.560
part is to get ultimate control over these users.&nbsp;
This is why they’re able to demand ridiculous sums&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:06.360
of money like $20 billion from Google every single&nbsp;
year. But it looks like they’ve got something else&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.360 --> 00:10:11.820
up their sleeve as well: an ad platform. Now,&nbsp;
there have been rumors about this for several&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:18.480
months but at this point, an ad platform is almost&nbsp;
a confirmed fact. If you look up ads on Apple’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:24.840
careers page, you get 75 results. Distinguished&nbsp;
Engineer ad platforms. Engineering Manager,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:31.500
ad platforms. Senior Product Manger, ad platforms.&nbsp;
They’re not even trying to hide it. They’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:37.440
literally calling it an ad platform themself.&nbsp;
And I cannot understate just how powerful this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:42.540
is. Google and Facebook have literally managed&nbsp;
to build trillion dollar companies around just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:48.240
serving ads and that’s based on a much more&nbsp;
generic userbase. Apple, on the other hand, has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:54.060
a highly concentrated userbase of well off people&nbsp;
because well they’re phones cost a lot of money.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.720 --> 00:11:01.620
In fact, the median household income of an&nbsp;
iPhone user is $85,000 and that was as of 2014.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.160 --> 00:11:07.740
By now, this number is likely over a $100,000&nbsp;
making iPhone users the absolute perfect target&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.740 --> 00:11:12.780
for ads. And given that Google and Facebook&nbsp;
can’t effectively market to these people,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:17.730
companies will have to go through Apple and&nbsp;
pay whatever stupid price they decide to go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.730 --> 00:11:22.860
with and this is really the endgame for&nbsp;
Apple. They’ve come to the realization&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:26.520
that they’ll probably never create a&nbsp;
product that’ll outsell the iPhone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:33.660
They also won’t be escaping iPhone dependency&nbsp;
anytime soon but maybe that’s not such a bad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:39.900
thing if they’re able to rethink the monetization&nbsp;
aspect. The key is to switch from depending on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.900 --> 00:11:47.700
iPhone sales to depending on iPhone usage because&nbsp;
while iPhone sales are going down, usage is only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.700 --> 00:11:52.680
going up. That’s exactly what they’ve been doing&nbsp;
with the App Store and their services and their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:58.200
predatory deals with Google and now their ad&nbsp;
platform. And given that these avenues are far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:02.640
more profitable than selling phones, Apple’s&nbsp;
income statements are only going to become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:08.820
more insane as they head towards becoming a $10&nbsp;
trillion giant. Apple has clearly just decided&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:08.820 --> 00:12:13.800
to embrace their dependency on the iPhone but&nbsp;
a tech company that has actually managed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:18.840
escape their dependency on their hero product is&nbsp;
Microsoft. Check out this video to learn more.

